# oracle-inputs: w12tip4p_long_water.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 7.4e-13, atoms 6.4e-12.
# oracle: pair_style hybrid (type pairs split): lj/cut/coul/long for O-O (atom-site Coulomb) and lj/cut/tip4p/long for O-H and H-H (M-site Coulomb; native refuses H-H outside the TIP4P sub-style), 27 rigid TIP4P/2005 waters, pppm/tip4p, shake 1e-10, 50 steps
# Measured with native LAMMPS: pair_style hybrid with the H-H pair outside the TIP4P sub-style stops with "ERROR: Water H epsilon must be 0.0 for pair style lj/cut/tip4p/long (src/KSPACE/pair_lj_cut_tip4p_long.cpp:519)", so the H-H pair stays with the TIP4P sub-style here. Measured max relative error, engine vs native: pe 3.7e-8, evdwl 1.9e-8, ecoul 1.9e-9, press 2.0e-7; x 2.4e-8, v 1.6e-6, f 2.3e-5.
units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
read_data       w12tip4p_long_water.data
pair_style      hybrid lj/cut/tip4p/long 1 2 1 1 0.1546 8.5 lj/cut/coul/long 8.5 8.5
pair_coeff      1 1 lj/cut/coul/long 0.1852 3.1589
pair_coeff      1 2 lj/cut/tip4p/long 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      2 2 lj/cut/tip4p/long 0.0 1.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 450.0 0.9572
angle_style     harmonic
angle_coeff     1 55.0 104.52
kspace_style    pppm/tip4p 1.0e-5
kspace_modify   gewald 0.37833912 mesh 12 12 12 order 5
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        1.0
fix             1 all shake 1.0e-10 200 0 b 1 a 1
fix             2 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             50
